            <ArticleTitle>An uncommon cause of abdominal pain in an adolescent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1065-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/SMJ.0b013e31817fe318</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Imperforate hymen is a rare congenital anomaly which emergency physicians often forget to include in the differential diagnosis of lower abdominal pain in a pubescent girl. These patients often remain asymptomatic until puberty and present in early adolescence with cyclic abdominal pain. This case report reviews the presentation and treatment of an 11-year-old girl with imperforate hymen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
